  "period_note": "Balance sheet is the period-end snapshot (reported), Solo basis, from First Security Islami Bank PLC's own Condensed Balance Sheet (Un-audited) as at 2025-06-30. Income-statement items with a '_cumulative' suffix are cumulative from 1 January of the same year; items with a '_discrete_q' suffix are the single discrete quarter alone -- both are printed directly as separate columns in the source document (not derived by subtraction), so both carry basis='reported'. OUTSIDE this dataset's core FY2011-2024 annual coverage; included as post-collapse trajectory context. The comparative prior-year-end Total Assets column in this filing cross-validates exactly (to the taka, after rounding) against this dataset's already-stored 691,205.74mn (2024_Q4.json) total_assets figure, confirming Solo basis continuity and no restatement between the audited annual figure and this interim filing's own comparative column. Filed/signed 2025-07-30. The crisis deepened further: Apr-Jun 2025 (discrete) Net Profit After Tax was BDT -11,170.09mn, even larger than Q1 2025's loss, pushing Solo Total Shareholders' Equity down to just BDT 3,143.31mn by 30-Jun-2025 -- roughly 26% of its BDT 12,081.39mn paid-up capital alone, i.e. the bank's capital base was already almost entirely eroded by mid-2025, months before Bangladesh Bank's Capital Reduction Order (dated 21-Dec-2025, effective 5-Nov-2025) formally wrote paid-up capital to zero. UNAUDITED. Some note-level figures (e.g. NAV per share ratio) could not be reliably parsed from this filing due to the deeply distorted (near-zero/negative) equity base breaking the usual note format; not included where extraction was not confident.",
